FILE: doc-component
FEATURE: component-module
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'component-teardown'

REASON
NEW FILE: doc/component.md, plus index and README updates.

The guide states the binding contract, both template forms, the full Component and
Instance surfaces, keyed lists, nesting, and the complete error list - every string
in which was captured from the running module rather than written from memory.

It also states plainly what the module will not become: no reactive state, no
computed properties, no expression language, no data-v-if or data-v-for. Recording
that in the guide rather than only in a changelog is deliberate, so the boundary
does not have to be re-argued every time someone asks for one more binding.

The 'Using it inside a custom element' section gives the six-line recipe for
wrapping a Component in a custom element, and warns against attaching a shadow root:
$$.ss/$$.sa are document.querySelector and stop at a shadow boundary, and every
stylesheet vUX loads goes to document.head where it cannot reach inside one.

doc/README.md gains the guide, the example and a short section on destroy().
README.md gains the two v4.0.0-beta feature bullets for this work; the rest of that
release's list was already empty and was left alone rather than reconstructed.


